Output:
## Implementation
- camel/memories/agent_memories.py
  - Classes: ChatHistoryMemory, VectorDBMemory, LongtermAgentMemory
  - Note: LongtermAgentMemory augments chat history with vector DB memory for persistent longterm memory.

- camel/toolkits/human_toolkit.py
  - Class: HumanToolkit
  - Functions: ask_human_via_console (two-way human interaction), send_message_to_user (one-way user message)
  - Provides human interaction tools for agents.

- camel/agents/chat_agent.py
  - Class: ChatAgent
  - Core agent class supporting memory, tools, toolkits, model management, summarization, and more.
  - Supports setting memory (including LongtermAgentMemory) and adding tools.

## Examples
- examples/agents/single_agent.py
  - Shows basic usage of ChatAgent with a prompt and model.
  - Useful as a template for creating single-agent scripts.

## Tests
- test/memories/test_agent_memories.py
  - Tests for LongtermAgentMemory and ChatHistoryMemory.
  - Useful for understanding expected behavior and usage patterns.

# Summary
To create an agent with longterm memory and human interaction tools, use:
- LongtermAgentMemory from camel.memories.agent_memories
- HumanToolkit from camel.toolkits.human_toolkit (for human interaction tools)
- ChatAgent from camel.agents.chat_agent

The example in examples/agents/single_agent.py shows basic agent creation and usage.

You can combine these to create your script at task-script/single_agent/9_longterm_memory_single_agent.py.
